@meta
id: 19-09
title: Once per file
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: cfdo
par: 115
minutes: 6
vscode: open each file from the results, paste the import at the top
vimrc: set hidden
open: README.md

@brief
`formatMoney` has moved into a shared package, and every file that
calls it needs `import { formatMoney } from '@shared/money';` as its
first line. The old local imports were removed in the last commit and
the new one was never added, so nothing compiles. Three files call it,
and two of them call it more than once.

`:cdo` runs once per hit. Run "add the import" through `:cdo` and the
files with two calls get two imports. `:cfdo` runs once per file in the
list, with the cursor on that file's first hit. Same list, different
granularity.

The command to run is `normal ggO` followed by the import line: go to
the top, open a line above, type. Two things to know. `:normal` takes
everything after it as keystrokes, including a `|`, so `| update`
cannot be chained onto it; write all the files afterwards with `:wa`
instead. And `hidden` is on for this lesson, so `:cfdo` can move
between modified buffers.

@keys
| `:cfdo cmd` | run `cmd` once per file in the quickfix list |
| `:cfdo %s/old/new/g \| update` | a whole-file substitute, once per file |
| `:cfdo normal keys` | normal-mode keys, once per file; `\|` is not a separator here |
| `:wa` | write every modified buffer |

@hints
`:vimgrep /formatMoney(/ **/*.ts`. Five hits in three files.
--
`:cfdo normal ggOimport { formatMoney } from '@shared/money';` and
Enter. Vim ends insert mode for you when `:normal` runs out of keys.
--
`:wa` then `:q`.

@solution
    :vimgrep /formatMoney(/ **/*.ts<Enter>
    :cfdo normal ggOimport { formatMoney } from '@shared/money';<Enter>
    :wa<Enter>  :q<Enter>

`:cdo` when the edit belongs to the hit line; `:cfdo` when it belongs
to the file. `:cfdo %s/old/new/g | update` is the common pairing: the
list chose the files, `%s` handles every line in each. For a plain
rename it gives the same result as `:cdo s/old/new/g | update`. It is
the one to reach for when the edit is not on the hit line at all: an
import at the top, a footer at the bottom, a `%s` that touches lines
the search did not.

`:normal` eating the bar is documented under `:help :bar`, together
with the other commands that do it, `:global` among them. It is why the
write here is a separate `:wa` and why `hidden` had to be on: with it
off, `:cfdo` would stop at the second file with E37, exactly as `:cdo`
did in lesson 5. `hidden` is on in your own vimrc, so in daily use this
just works; the lesson turned it off earlier so you would see why the
`| update` habit exists.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/configuration/registry.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from '../domain/order/order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from '../domain/order/order.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from '../domain/payment/payment.producer';
import { PaymentProvider } from '../domain/payment/payment.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

container.register(PaymentProducer, { useClass: PaymentProducer });
container.register(OrderRepository, { useClass: OrderRepository });
container.register(OrderProvider, { useClass: OrderProvider });
container.register(PaymentProvider, { useClass: PaymentProvider });
container.register(PaymentService, { useClass: PaymentService });

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async summary(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return {
      total: formatMoney(order.total),
      refundable: formatMoney(order.status === 'SHIPPED' ? 0 : order.total),
    };
  }
}

